   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Food and Agriculture Organization (FAO)</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Global Health Security (GHS) Project - Strengthening animal health, One Health, and antimicrobial resistance capacities to prevent and mitigate zoonotic threats in Uzbekistan</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The specific objectives of the GHS Program in Uzbekistan are:
- Strengthen national capacity for surveillance along critical nodes of the livestock value chains and readiness to prevent, early detect and respond effectively to animal and public health threats such as priority zoonotic diseases. This will be based on enhanced transparency, disease reporting, sample collection, shipment and processing, as well as data collection and data analysis at country level.
- Improve the above-mentioned capacities of the national veterinary system through policy review and policy implementation, the strengthening of emergency response systems, with particular emphasis on biosecurity, laboratory diagnosis and surveillance.
- AMR: effective multisectoral coordination on AMR.
- Initiate or increase public?private partnership work between stakeholders involved in addressing animal health threats, including emerging, re-emerging and endemic zoonoses, to enhance preparedness, early detection, response and control.</narrative>
  </description>
